Parameters:

Methods can have parameters. This is the additional information the method requires to use in its tasks.
Parameters are defined in a comma separated list found within the method's parenthesis. They must specify a data type followed by its identifier. 

	public void methodName(type parameter1, type parameter2){
		System.out.println(parameter1, parameter2);
	}

During the method call, the number of arguments must match the number of parameters along with the parameter's data type.

Import statements:

To import a class from another package, you must explicitly import by indicating the package name followed by its class name. E.g. import package.class.method;
If the class is within the same package, these classes are implicitly imported.
You don't need to do a declaration if you refer the class by its fully quantified class name.